GO/NO-GO READ:
  * mean(all) signal_sd >> single(n0), reliability clears ~0.3-0.4  -> all-neuron arm has
    a gen-0 toehold single-neuron missed; worth an overnight.
  * mean(all) ~ single(n0), both flat, #-above-chance uniform across genomes -> no toehold;
    RL-in-development (which can manufacture a gradient the unsupervised floor cannot) is
    the better structural lever.
  * best(all) high but mean(all) flat -> lucky-neuron lottery (rises with in-degree at
    fixed N); NOT a selectable signal on its own -- do not be fooled by best alone.
